answer:
Mondays bloom with foolish joy;  
A morning quilt and plump hush.  
Do not ask for coffins, pass;  
A stack of tasks is all you rush.  

A chill wind cuts through a chill grin;  
A blizzard calls for a plain bun.  
A short chat, a cup of warm min;  
A ritual that will pay roundly on sun.  

Mondays cloak a gloomy grin;  
A lad with a soul all on his shin.  
No room for faults, no room for hur;  
A doll's play and a pudding for a rush.

